      "round_summary": "Repair-round 2: fixed assertion_error for no_counter_underflow. Root cause: the original assertion `!(mode === 1.U && io.i && cnt === 0.U)` forbids the legitimate reachable state where cnt has just decremented to 0 while io.i remains high. The design's guard `io.i && (cnt =/= 0.U)` correctly prevents actual underflow (wrapping from 0 to 4095). Fix: replace the overly strict combinatorial condition with a temporal check using RegNext — sample `mode === 1.U && io.i && cnt === 0.U` into `underflow_danger`, then assert that when underflow_danger was true last cycle, cnt must not be non-zero this cycle (i.e., cnt must stay at 0 and not wrap). This detects real underflow while allowing the legitimate cnt=0 state. Preserved original assertion label `no_counter_underflow`. No homologous assertions found (only one assertion with this label in the file).",
